{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779592360,"nonce":"DAdR2LHL8/mSbFF+02j+qbrqbyA=","message":"Implementation follow-up before fixing template drag/drop: current Templates sidebar inserts template-backed components as opaque/cached subgraph nodes. In the IAB this can replace/annihilate the current graph level or leave a purple node with inconsistent fold/enter-subgraph behavior, and subsequent normal component drops can queue until reload. Intended behavior for this issue is different: dragging a template should import/expand the template's graph non-destructively into the current graph level at the drop point. Any subgraph nodes contained inside the template should remain ordinary descendable subgraph nodes; the template itself should not become an inaccessible opaque wrapper by default. I am going to fix the canvas/graphStore insertion path to expand template graphs into the active graph level and add regression coverage for non-destructive insertion.","files":null}]}